## Overview

This is a Spring PetClinic REST project using the OpenAPI generator pattern: the HTTP mapping (`@RequestMapping`, `@Valid`, `@RequestBody`) lives on a generated interface (`OwnersApi`), which the hand-written `OwnerRestControllerV1` implements. The V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) has no POST, only a paged GET, so the create endpoint is V1's `addOwner`.

---

## 1. The @RestController method handling POST /api/owners

The mapping is split across two files.

### Request mapping + `@Valid` — generated interface
`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`

Lines 52, 79-87 define the POST mapping and body validation:
```java
