## 7. Spring Security relevant to this endpoint

### Method-level authorization
`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` is annotated `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` (line 99). `@roles` resolves to the `Roles` bean:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java` (lines 5-11)
```java
@Component
public class Roles {
    public final String OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN";
    ...
}
```
So `hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (`hasRole` with a value already prefixed `ROLE_` matches that authority directly.)

### Security filter chains — toggled by the `petclinic.security.enable` property
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java` (active when `petclinic.security.enable=true`): `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)` (line 19) is what makes `@PreAuthorize` take effect; CSRF disabled; `anyRequest().authenticated()` with HTTP Basic; JDBC-backed users/roles (lines 48-53); `BCryptPasswordEncoder` bean (lines 26-29).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java` (active when `petclinic.security.enable=false`): CSRF disabled and `anyRequest().permitAll()`. Note this config does **not** enable method security, so when security is disabled the `@PreAuthorize` is effectively inert and the endpoint is open.

