## Full call chain summary

1. `POST /api/owners` → mapping from `OwnersApi.addOwner` (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`); Bean Validation runs on the DTO (`@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Size`/`@Email`/custom `@TelephoneValidation`); failures → 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.
2. `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (enforced only when `BasicAuthenticationConfig` is active).
3. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` → new `Owner`, telephone normalized to E.164, email lower-cased, `id`/`pets` ignored.
4. `clinicService.isTelephoneInUse(...)` (readOnly tx, scans all owners) → 409 if duplicate.
5. If `sharesHousehold != true`, `clinicService.isHouseholdInUse(lastName, address)` (readOnly tx) → 409 if duplicate household.
6. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (read-write tx): sets `customerCode` if null (counts all owners), then `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
7. Repository `save` → `em.persist` (new entity) → `@PrePersist onCreate()` defaults `registrationDate` to today → INSERT into `owners`.
8. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` (adds `displayName`, `initials`), `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, HTTP 201.
